{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1020","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1020","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1020\",\"parent_revision\":\"497af9e3d9c65c6d83277ecdd4c27eb8aa134a23\",\"root_revision\":\"09d4a08b56d87f02b6041f91f11bb737e63f7e1674e58682c6a72bf952dfa05f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P0\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe backlog_core GraphQL layer has 11 call sites to _fetch_issues_graphql across operations.py, server.py, and github.py. Only 1 of 11 callers (refresh_local_cache_from_github) uses the since parameter for incremental sync. The other 10 fetch all issues every time. Additionally, 3 functions have N+1 patterns where they loop and call _fetch_issue_graphql (single-issue fetch) per item instead of using the bulk result: backlog_normalize (operations.py:1830), backlog_groom (operations.py:2266), and create_issue_with_body (github.py:1060/1090). The fetch-process-track pattern is duplicated across all 11 call sites instead of being a shared primitive.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **extract shared graphql sync primitive for bulk fetch with incremental since filtering** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation - 2026-03-22 GraphQL efficiency audit after issues 916 and 1018\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|